<para>solve the expression augmented with an additional explicit rhs term (e.g. the momentum predictor&apos;s -grad(p)). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The owned system ls_ is assembled once and solved in place. The extra rhs term is applied to ls_.rhs() only for the duration of the solve and then removed again, so ls_ is left holding the rhs-free (&quot;H&quot;) system that the subsequent rAU/HbyA step expects. This avoids deep-copying the whole momentum LinearSystem — its nnz x Vec3 matrix values plus the boundary and off-diagonal matrices — on every momentum solve; only the rhs (which is identical in shape to the owned one) is touched. The solver treats the system rhs as read-only, so restoring it by adding the source back matches the previous copy-based behaviour. (WR-2) </para>
